<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids remained mostly lower on Friday in tandem with weaker Minneapolis futures prices.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, a lot of winter and spring wheat was moved as farmers capitalized on the prices, Montana dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think farmers wanted to sell late last week and early this week,&quot; a Montana merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Soft white wheat bids were also weaker. &quot;Portland came down in line with a weaker futures market,&quot; an Oregon dealer said.</p>
<p>MGE March wheat lost 5-1/4 cents to end at $3.78 a bushel.  </p>
